<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10954" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνώμο-τος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμνυμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unsworn, not bound by oath,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γλῶσσ᾽ ὀμώμοχ᾽, ἡ δὲ φρὴν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					612
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μάρτυρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					5.12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.86
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ἀνώμοτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					737
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					<u>Or.</u>
					28(49).94
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not sworn to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρήνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					19.204
				</span></i>
			.</div>
